  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "First to the ball",
  "description": "Two lines side by side some way from a goal, with a slalom of cones in front of each line. One player from each line runs the slalom. At the same time the coach passes a ball into the space between the courses. Whoever reaches the ball first shoots at goal; the other tries to stop the shot. Afterwards, join the back of your own line.\n\nVariation: instead of the slalom, run around a cone and then to the ball. Works well for young children, from about 7 years old. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Take short, quick steps between the cones."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look up for the ball as you come out of the course."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "First to the ball: take it towards goal and shoot straight away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Second to the ball: get between the ball and the goal."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 1,
